            <div class="nature-copy">
                <h2>Nature &amp; Culture of Malaysia</h2>
                <p>From the cloud-kissed spine of Borneo to the misty Cameron Highlands, Malaysia's landscapes feel like a living museum. Every ridgeline, river, and reef threads into rituals, folklore, and food.</p>
                <p>Kinabalu rises as Southeast Asia's rooftop, Taman Negara shelters 130-million-year-old rainforest, and island reefs glow with bioluminescent blues. These wild places aren't just scenic backdrops - they shape festivals, ingredients, and the rhythm of village life.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="tapestry-section">
            <div class="tapestry-copy">
                <h2>A Tapestry of Cultures</h2>
                <p>Malay wayang kulit, Chinese lanterns, Indian bharatanatyam rhythms, and indigenous Gawai harvest songs intermingle on the same streets. Diversity here isn't a slogan - it's the soundtrack of everyday life.</p>
                <p>Morning markets trade nasi lemak beside dim sum steamers; Fridays call the faithful to mosques, temples, and churches often within a single block. Shared celebrations like Hari Raya, Lunar New Year, Deepavali, and Kaamatan keep the nation dancing in unison.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tapestry-media">
                <img src="/public/images/bendera.jpg" alt="Traditional culture of Malaysia" class="tapestry-main">
            </div>
        </section>

